# README EN->CS Sync Rule

When updating the root English README, keep the Czech README aligned in the same change.

## Required sync behavior

- If `README.md` changes in content, structure, commands, links, or setup steps, update `README.cs.md` accordingly.
- Preserve the same section order and headings hierarchy in both files.
- Translate explanatory prose to Czech, but keep commands, paths, environment variable names, URLs, and code blocks unchanged unless the English source changed them.
- Keep language switch links at the top of both files:
  - `README.md`: `English | [Čeština](README.cs.md)`
  - `README.cs.md`: `[English](README.md) | Čeština`

## Verification before finishing

- Confirm both files include equivalent key sections (setup, run, tests, deployment, related docs).
- Confirm critical commands and env vars match exactly between the two files.
- Treat README language drift as a documentation bug.
